  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 100 PM CDT Thu May 7 2026\n\nTemperatures are running about 10 to 15 degrees warmer than this \ntime yesterday, with some Cu popping across central Minnesota. Did \nbump temperatures up a few degrees and dewpoints down a couple \ndegrees to account for the better mixing as advertised in model\nsoundings both today and tomorrow. This will allow RH values to\nfall to 25 to 20 percent, particularly for western Minnesota. \nHowever, fairly light winds are keeping critical fire weather \nconcerns at bay. Another round of near freezing temperatures are\nexpected tonight, but increasing cloud cover moving in from the\nDakotas will help keep temperatures in check across western and\nsouthern Minnesota. While it's borderline, did decide to go \nahead with another Frost Advisory for western Wisconsin into far\neast central Minnesota. We should get a break from the frost \nconcerns for at least a day or two, with colder overnight lows \nbriefly returning Sunday and Monday morning. \n\nTemperatures tomorrow should reach the upper 60s to low 70s as we \nget a break from what has felt like constant cold air advection. As \nmentioned above, RH values are expected to fall to around 25 \npercent. Winds will be a little stronger tomorrow, which could lead \nto elevated fire weather concerns. An approaching cold front will \nbring isolated shower chances during the evening to west central \nMinnesota, but the bulk of any rain chances will hold off until \nafter midnight into early Saturday morning. The best chance for \nprecip will be across central Minnesota and western Wisconsin, but \neven then, QPF amounts are only a few hundredths at best. Following \nthe FROPA, highs for the weekend will be back in the 50s and 60s \nwith breezy northwest winds. \n\nAs we head into early next week, it will finally start feeling more \nMay-like with a warming trend expected to take hold through the \nweek. The 500mb low that seems to have been stuck over Hudson Bay \nfinally begins to drift eastward late Sunday. Another trough will \nswing through early Tuesday, bringing another brief cool down and \nsome shower chances to the region. Once that system moves through, \nwe'll see temperatures continue to climb with highs in the upper 70s \nto low 80s possible by this time next week.",
